  "note": "Triennial urban council election of May 1949. No newspaper report has been found; the Belfast and Ulster Directory 1950 (compiled after the election) lists the nine members of the council. Nine members printed (chairman Ed. M'Cavana, J.P.; vice-chairman W. G. Kearney, J.P.), matching the nine seats. Directory list, not an election report: the directory prints the council's membership as it stood when the edition was compiled (late in the year after the election). It does not say whether members were returned at a poll or unopposed, and cannot show co-options made between the election and compilation. No votes."
